{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 40, :comments ["<b>For I lift up to the heavens, etc.</b> This is the language of an oath — that He swore by the lifting up of His hand to whet His sword to avenge Himself on His enemies. And this is His saying ״אִם שַׁנּוֹתִי בְּרַק״ and so forth, and His saying ״וְתֹאחֵז בְּמִשְׁפָּט</b> — meaning, it is strengthened through the attribute of strict judgment." "<b>Or</b> it may further intend that the attribute of mercy will also concur and be strengthened in judgment to bring vengeance upon the enemies of HaShem — who are the enemies of Israel — for they hate us only because of our clinging to HaShem. And He says ״וְלִמְשַׂנְאַי״ — they are the sect that causes Israel to transgress the faith."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:21:41.709141041Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}